/// Transcript — the REPL's shared log, and a day-0 convenience elsewhere (ADR 0129 §5).
///
/// `Transcript` is a sealed, stateless class whose API is entirely class-side.
/// It has no instance, no stream protocol and no capture API.
///
/// Programs should use `Logger` (ADR 0064), or `Console` for plain
/// stdout/stderr. `Transcript` exists for newcomers and REPL use:
///
/// | Selector | In an interactive workspace | Elsewhere |
/// |---|---|---|
/// | `show:` | Appends the value's text to the workspace's `TranscriptStream` | One Logger `notice` event, domain `[beamtalk, user, transcript]` |
/// | `cr` | Appends a newline | No-op |
/// | `showCr:` | `show:` then `cr` | One Logger event |
/// | `recent` | The buffered lines | Raises `no_workspace` |
/// | `clear` | Empties the buffer | Raises `no_workspace` |
///
/// The Logger route prints plain text, one line per event, under `beamtalk run`,
/// `beamtalk test` and in releases. Two consecutive `show:` sends are two
/// events, not one line. Ordering relative to `Console`, which writes
/// synchronously, is not guaranteed. Capturing, silencing or redirecting the
/// output is ordinary Logger configuration on the transcript domain.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// Transcript showCr: "Hello"
/// Transcript show: "a"; cr; show: "b"
/// Transcript recent
/// ```
sealed typed Object subclass: Transcript native: beamtalk_transcript_facade

  /// Write a value: a String as-is, anything else as its printString.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Transcript show: "hello"
  /// Transcript show: 42
  /// ```
  class sealed show: value :: Object -> Nil => self delegate

  /// Write a newline. A no-op outside an interactive workspace.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Transcript cr
  /// ```
  class sealed cr -> Nil => self delegate

  /// Write a value followed by a newline.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Transcript showCr: "hello"
  /// ```
  class sealed showCr: value :: Object -> Nil => self delegate

  /// Return the recent transcript lines. Raises `no_workspace` when there is
  /// no interactive workspace's transcript.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Transcript recent
  /// ```
  class sealed recent -> List(String) => self delegate

  /// Empty the transcript buffer. Raises `no_workspace` when there is no
  /// interactive workspace's transcript.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// Transcript clear
  /// ```
  class sealed clear -> Nil => self delegate
